  "title": "Continuing the story of early DOS development",
  "summary": "In 2018 we (re)-open-sourced MS‑DOS 1.25 and 2.11 and in 2024 we were able to make the source for MS‑DOS 4.0 available to the public. Today, on 86-DOS 1.00’s 45th anniversary, we’re continuing that tradition with the earliest DOS source code discovered to date.",
